<title>USA: National Semiconductor revises 1997 Q2, Q3.</title>
<headline>National Semiconductor revises 1997 Q2, Q3.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA CLARA, Calif. 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in millions, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>		Second Quarter			Third Quarter</p>
<p>		    Three Mos		  Three Mos     Nine Mos</p>
<p>			 Ended			 Ended	  Ended</p>
<p>	   Nov. 24, 1996	     Feb. 23, 1997  Feb. 23, 1997</p>
<p>As Reported:</p>
<p> Gross Margin	$230.8		     $255.3	 $658.3</p>
<p> Gross Margin %     34.9%			37.5%	  34.5%</p>
<p> Restructuring	    0			    0	  256.3</p>
<p> Net Income (loss)   29.5			 42.8     ( 135.3)</p>
<p>Earnings (loss)</p>
<p>  per share	     .21			  .30	 ( .97)</p>
<p>As Revised:</p>
<p> Gross Margin	 248.1			282.4	  702.7</p>
<p> Gross Margin %     37.5%			41.5%	  36.8%</p>
<p> Restructuring	    0		    (192.0)	   64.3</p>
<p> Net Income	    42.5			207.1	   42.0</p>
<p>Earnings per</p>
<p>  share		   .30			 1.39	    .30</p>
<p>NOTE: Results were revised in response to a Securities and Exchange Commission review of the company's spin-off of its Fairchild businesses. The revision reflects the company's recognition of $192 million in recovery of Fairchild restructuring reserves in the third quarter of 1997 and $9 million in the fourth quarter of $1997, instead of $201 in the fourth quarter, as previously announced. In the revised earnings, the company is also reversing a depreciation expense, resulting in a $17 million increase in gross margin and pre-tax earnings in the second and third quarters and a $3 million increase in the fourth quarter.</p>
<p>The revision will not affect full year earnings.</p>
</text>
